                <pb facs="0561" n="481" xml:id="pg481"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Sickles.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-06-28"><hi rendition="#italic">June 28,
                        1901</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hill directs the issue of such papers as will be accepted by the Spanish
                    authorities for the present to insure the registration of Cubans and Porto
                    Ricans as under the protection of the United States, but not as citizens
                    thereof.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
